    "explanation": "Both parties: this is the Bugis Junction to Jurong East trip of 7 Aug 2026, TRP-00114. The distance question is settled by the trace. POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing measurement, and it reads 23.97 km against a booked optimal of 18.0 km, an excess of 5.97 km or 33.17% of optimal. Both establishment tests pass (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is not MATERIAL, being under both the 50% and the 8.0 km gates, so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not engaged; in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 1 (below 3) and 1 divided by completed_trips_90d of 412 is far below 0.05, so no repeat pattern exists and no conduct referral arises. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is a near-synonym and has not been used.\n\nThe driver's account that the AYE was crawling from the Alexandra exit and that the PIE detour was faster is an external-traffic assertion. Under POL-RD-13 it is tested against the traffic_advisory for this trip and nothing else. The bundle holds no such advisory: EV-ADVIS-00114-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT. That comparison cannot be run, POL-RD-03 is unavailable, and the assertion carries no weight under POL-RD-08. It neither reduces the measured excess nor supplies an adjusted optimal. Because the driver named no advisory identifier, this is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) does not escalate the case (POL-RD-13(1)), and POL-RD-13(2) directs that the deviation stand at the measured figure with POL-RD-02 run against the booked optimal route.\n\nNo distance is excluded. The only rider message is a question, 'adam road?? jurong is the other way', not an instruction, and derived.waypoint_approach.messages is empty, so POL-RD-04 does not apply. No pickup or dropoff amendment engages POL-RD-05, and the vehicle type RYDE_X puts POL-RD-12 out of play.\n\nThe refund is arithmetic under POL-RD-02 on the METERED fare. The surge multiplier of 1.6 is read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier on EV-FARE-00114, the only artifact that carries it, and the rider does not contest it. recomputed_fare = ((3.80 base + 0.75 x 18.0 km + 0.28 x 30.0 min) x 1.6) + 0.80 platform fee + 2.50 ERP on the optimal route = 44.42. charged_total is 58.10. Refund = 58.10 - 44.42 = 13.68, rounded up on the payable figure to SGD 13.70.\n\nOn ERP: both billed gantries were genuinely crossed. The trace passes 0.0 m from the Kim Keat Link towards Tuas gantry (on the optimal route, 2.50) and 8.76 m from the Adam Rd towards Tuas gantry (off the optimal route, 2.00), both inside the 250 m match radius, so neither is a phantom line and no billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4) is warranted. The off-route 2.00 is already comprehended in the POL-RD-02 refund, because the recomputed fare includes only the on-optimal-route gantry; it is itemised here for transparency and is not added on top.\n\nThe rider's contested figure is not what the policy supports: the arithmetic yields 13.70, not 15.00. The refund is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and at 23.5% of charged_total, well below the 90% share that would convert it to a full refund, so the outcome is a partial refund. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifiers match on trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, the trace is unbroken (241 fixes at a 10 s interval, max gap 0.0, so POL-RD-07(a) to (c) is not met), timestamps agree, and every charge line has a trace counterpart. Confidence is 0.9, the deciding facts resting on artifacts at weight 1.0 (EV-GPS-00114, EV-TRIP-00114, EV-FARE-00114). The monetary effect is 13.70, above the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so this ruling issues but the amount is held for release rather than executed on issue."
  },
